# Javascript "classes"

No `class` keyword. Reusable objects are factory arrow functions: private state in a local `data` object, methods as inner arrow functions, return an object literal exposing the public API.

```javascript
const Prompt = ({ prompt }) => {
  const data = Object.create(null)
  data.prompt = prompt

  const expand = () => {
    // expansion logic
  }

  const toString = () => {
    return data.prompt
  }

  return {
    expand,
    toString,
    getPrompt: () => data.prompt
  }
}
```
